<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Typhōeus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ),
		ĕos, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυφωεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a giant</i>, <i>struck with lightning
				by Jupiter and buried under Mount Ætna</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 9,
				716</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5, 321 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4,
				491</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 4, 53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 14,
				196 al.</span></i>—As a gigantic monster, called
			centimanus, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3, 303</span></i>. —Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Typhōĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Typhōeus</i>, <i>Typhœan</i> tela, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1,
				665</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cervix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 3, 183</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Typhōïs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj f.</i>, <i>of Typhōeus</i>, <i>Typhœan</i>: Aetna, Ov H. 15, 11.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
